#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119550 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "b25256b2-09fe-5faa-b27a-bfea7654e8ef" :question/math-academy-id "e-3019" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} [  3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) ] \\,\\textrm{d}t$ given that $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 16, \\: 2,\\: -2\\right\\rangle$ and $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2}\\mathbf g(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 2,-4,2\\right\\rangle .$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t =  \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3f(t)+g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨16,\\,2,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨48,\\,6,\\,-6⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨50,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119551 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "5c4164d7-605a-597c-9bab-f6599becc527" :question/math-academy-id "e-3020" :question/problem "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\: 1, \\: 3 \\right\\rangle$\nand\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 0, \\: 2, \\: 6 \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t+\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t = \n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t - \\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6⟩-⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119552 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "1d356bbb-b4ad-5730-9bd1-7f3cd151f96f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3021" :question/problem "Find $\\displaystyle {\\int_0^1 }  \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t)  \\, \\textrm d t$ \ngiven that \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm d t = \\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k$ \nand \n$\\mathbf c=\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k .$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t =  \\mathbf c \\times {\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t  .\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(j-k)\\times (i-3\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-4-3)i-(0+1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =-7\\,i-\\,j-\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119698 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/id #uuid "40927582-03c4-5dcb-b2cc-7c68c73388b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8688" :question/problem "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2\\mathbf f(t) + \\langle 1,\\:-1,\\:1\\rangle\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_2^0\\mathbf f(t) \\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle -3, \\: 2, \\: 1 \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨t,\\,-t,\\,t⟩{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨2,\\,-2,\\,2⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,-4,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6088ac3-62a3-55f9-9254-bd3af6af7de0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-2,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388029} {:answer/id #uuid "a26c5fac-577d-55ea-8c59-6e164ae1455b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388030} {:answer/id #uuid "bb49ba41-a2a8-57f8-98f2-980a02993f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,4,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388031} {:answer/id #uuid "adc83598-1819-58a2-a620-584ae08d2974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,-2,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388032} {:answer/id #uuid "c06243b2-433d-5357-a811-c37305881773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-4,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6088ac3-62a3-55f9-9254-bd3af6af7de0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-2,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388029} :answer-field/id #uuid "8df1086a-a10d-51ec-be27-8b1ada17a1b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b77f59d-ad05-5d0e-a768-18e851546b1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129266" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-1,\\,3,\\,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-1,\\,3,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-3,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{0}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-3,\\,2⟩+⟨t,\\,-t,\\,0⟩{|}_{1}^{0} \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-3,\\,2⟩+⟨-1,\\,1,\\,0⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440630 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb8259f-8c90-5906-950d-4eceda1af95a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,1,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440580} {:answer/id #uuid "3577fefa-4330-511f-bfb5-e3b0bdd5b2d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,5,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440585} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb2546e-95e7-5c4f-8882-4b1f0f221022" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,3,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440598} {:answer/id #uuid "a45f0695-37ea-5976-9377-b321aab76838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,-5,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440601} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf3598f-9c3e-57f6-8286-eee1de57ab13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,-1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cb8259f-8c90-5906-950d-4eceda1af95a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,1,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440580} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ce4d30d-9663-5cde-be1f-6bc470206c3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47592607-bdfd-5d8e-9c5b-5217893655c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-129271" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨15,\\,3,\\,6⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨12,\\,2,\\,4⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨15,\\,3,\\,6⟩-⟨12,\\,2,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0735890c-3c78-543f-89dd-6ca5377bb2e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,i+17\\,j-12\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440570} {:answer/id #uuid "4be058a2-5710-5ff7-a820-882c2fc11385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,i+7\\,j-24\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440587} {:answer/id #uuid "4eafeb6b-988b-5aa2-8275-39f0afff0b14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11\\,i+15\\,j-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440588} {:answer/id #uuid "9797327b-29d3-5967-8722-3e2bb5aa98ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15\\,i+16\\,j-24\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440597} {:answer/id #uuid "a78142dc-7eec-57bb-a2d3-d7dcffeea81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,i+17\\,j+23\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a78142dc-7eec-57bb-a2d3-d7dcffeea81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,i+17\\,j+23\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440603} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd206ea4-1fa4-5b1a-b95a-d7f9dcd15b33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9dfd8a34-cf86-59cc-aba6-9a0a73cfe2af" :question/math-academy-id "q-129296" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=7\\,i-4\\,j-k$ \nand \n$c=3\\,i-5\\,j+2\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(3\\,i-5\\,j+2\\,k)\\times (7\\,i-4\\,j-k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 7 & -4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5+8)i-(-3-14)j+(-12+35)k \\\\  & =13\\,i+17\\,j+23\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302176 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f98e94d-1058-57cf-8d27-f13954103a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300023} {:answer/id #uuid "316106c6-12a5-5e17-af69-75de97025a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300204} {:answer/id #uuid "b73bae5f-1557-57a4-b715-8b64982c76c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300877} {:answer/id #uuid "eef1692d-2f31-59e3-870d-7b705a603ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301146} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc4d73d-2ea8-5c78-a393-c5faf89cb3ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b73bae5f-1557-57a4-b715-8b64982c76c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300877} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa59178e-27aa-5b8c-b124-8431df83afc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "abace35f-02da-57bf-9b60-2e1f0caa0d18" :question/math-academy-id "q-32511" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})\\,i+{e}^{2}\\,j+(2{e}^{-1}-3{e}^{-2})\\,k$ \nand \n$c={e}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{-2}\\,j-{e}^{2}\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({e}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{-2}\\,j-{e}^{2}\\,k)\\cdot (({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})\\,i+{e}^{2}\\,j+(2{e}^{-1}-3{e}^{-2})\\,k) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}\\cdot ({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})+{e}^{-2}\\cdot {e}^{2}-{e}^{2}\\cdot (2{e}^{-1}-3{e}^{-2}) \\\\  & =e-1+1-2e+3 \\\\  & =3-e.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c143a77-e1af-52aa-b7eb-98785edc55ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i+2j+24k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440571} {:answer/id #uuid "1f61aaf4-763c-5aa0-8b51-415ad9b6527c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+2j-24k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440581} {:answer/id #uuid "56eb2684-dae3-5d7e-affd-236ebbf2899e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i-2j+8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440589} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc32dcc-74ea-50ee-823d-5aefc081089d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i+2j-8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440608} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6245d5-3350-59d5-9f2f-1fe8e4fa79d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+2j+8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f61aaf4-763c-5aa0-8b51-415ad9b6527c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+2j-24k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440581} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac63dd9f-32cd-5ec8-8fb2-52c021ed5db9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e79507a4-566e-5fff-acc4-da31b5f94ddb" :question/math-academy-id "q-32521" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=16\\,i+8\\,j+2\\,k$ \nand \n$c=-i+j.$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-i+j)\\times (16\\,i+8\\,j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 8 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 16 & 8\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(-2-0)j+(-8-16)k \\\\  & =2i+2j-24k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46bf7675-80a2-559b-8162-709a1a0d7f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,\\,6,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358358} {:answer/id #uuid "52b55dd5-256e-5209-86de-a9c9700d2990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,\\,2,\\,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358461} {:answer/id #uuid "90b044f6-737d-5f41-adc8-0bdca392f181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359017} {:answer/id #uuid "e6dcc4aa-84e5-52fb-b4ea-896d476393a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9,\\,1,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359794} {:answer/id #uuid "ec412725-0d94-59a0-8fbf-bf17919c936a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,-3,\\,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90b044f6-737d-5f41-adc8-0bdca392f181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359017} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3e28b5a-b897-5ddd-a2bd-d85b9a72bf4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29982efe-8588-56f9-8a2e-657a512dab79" :question/math-academy-id "q-96943" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩-⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f78597b-fe94-5d3b-a150-9662a2903e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,\\,2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395460} {:answer/id #uuid "54233a06-2e66-5ab0-bfb0-15ca60c09e48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,\\,4,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395461} {:answer/id #uuid "2f8ee068-02df-52c1-8b28-1bce069cc447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,\\,4,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395462} {:answer/id #uuid "4dc8b035-a308-57f9-911c-85c571aca7df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395463} {:answer/id #uuid "522f82da-1bbc-554e-89ea-d20bd82ed703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,-2,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f8ee068-02df-52c1-8b28-1bce069cc447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,\\,4,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395462} :answer-field/id #uuid "41b5d00f-231c-5d5e-9824-656cae587369" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6362c37-2e32-54b3-8aa0-c3cb9e6d3761" :question/math-academy-id "q-98186" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)+⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{3}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨5,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{3}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨5,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,\\,1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)+⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{3}⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-5,\\,1,\\,2⟩+{⟨-t,\\,t,\\,-t⟩|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =⟨-5,\\,1,\\,2⟩+⟨-3,\\,3,\\,-3⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨-8,\\,4,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
